{"name":"Best in Show","hex":"#b9b7bd","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"best","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["superlative form of good: most good.","Most; largest."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["superlative form of well: most well","To the most advantage; with the most success, cause, profit, benefit, or propriety."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/best"},{"term":"show","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To display, convey or exhibit; to have something available for others to see; to direct attention to something.","To indicate; to convey facts that lead to a conclusion."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A play, dance, or other entertainment.","An exhibition of items."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/show"}],"entries":[{"title":"Best in Show (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Best in Show is a 2000 American mockumentary comedy film co-written by Christopher Guest and Eugene Levy and directed by Guest. The film follows five entrants in a prestigious dog show as they travel to and compete at the show, and stars Guest and Levy alongside Jennifer Coolidge, John Michael Higgins, Michael Hitchcock, Jane Lynch, Michael McKean, Catherine O'Hara, and Parker Posey. Much of the dialogue was improvised. Many of the comic actors were also involved in Guest's other films, including Waiting for Guffman, A Mighty Wind, For Your Consideration, and Mascots. The film's score was composed by C. J. Vanston."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/43/BestInShow2000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_in_Show_(film)","wikidata":"Q830324"},{"title":"Best in Show (Grinspoon album)","blocks":[{"text":"Best in Show is a compilation album by Australian post-grunge band Grinspoon. The album was released on 7 November 2005 to coincide with the ten-year anniversary of the band.\nThe album peaked at No. 12 on the ARIA Albums Chart and was certified Gold. The first track, \"Sweet as Sugar\", was specially recorded for this album and, appropriately, is a return to the earlier style of the band. The rest of the tracks are listed chronologically, from \"Champion\", recorded in 1996, to \"Hard Act to Follow\", recorded in 2004. The liner notes contain photography of the band from their beginnings to the present, and details the history of the band in the form of a fairy tale about the 'Knights of Grinspoon' from the 'Land of Oz'. The limited edition bonus disc includes a collection of covers recorded over the years."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/49/Best_in_Show_%28Grinspoon_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_in_Show_(Grinspoon_album)","wikidata":"Q4896862"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"best":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/En-us-best.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3a/En-us-best.ogg/En-us-best.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/En-au-best.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b5/En-au-best.ogg/En-au-best.ogg.mp3"}],"show":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/En-us-show.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/43/En-us-show.ogg/En-us-show.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/En-uk-to_show.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ea/En-uk-to_show.ogg/En-uk-to_show.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey bucchero-ware bowl, Clay, 1000-700 BCE, Nr. Babakõy, Turkey, Fitzwilliam Museum, Cambridge","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg/500px-Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg","ratio":0.8,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl,_Clay,_1000-700_BCE,_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y,_Turkey,_Fitzwilliam_Museum,_Cambridge.jpg","share":0.248125},{"title":"Caeberllan Cawrfab 7fed', the best Welsh Black bullock in Smithfield Show, London 1973 (1519765)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Caeberllan_Cawrfab_7fed%27%2C_the_best_Welsh_Black_bullock_in_Smithfield_Show%2C_London_1973_%281519765%29.jpg/500px-Caeberllan_Cawrfab_7fed%27%2C_the_best_Welsh_Black_bullock_in_Smithfield_Show%2C_London_1973_%281519765%29.jpg","ratio":1.5233333333333334,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caeberllan_Cawrfab_7fed%27,_the_best_Welsh_Black_bullock_in_Smithfield_Show,_London_1973_(1519765).jpg","share":0.223125},{"title":"Caeberllan Cawrfab 7fed', the best Welsh Black bullock in Smithfield Show, London 1973 (1519770)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Caeberllan_Cawrfab_7fed%27%2C_the_best_Welsh_Black_bullock_in_Smithfield_Show%2C_London_1973_%281519770%29.jpg/500px-Caeberllan_Cawrfab_7fed%27%2C_the_best_Welsh_Black_bullock_in_Smithfield_Show%2C_London_1973_%281519770%29.jpg","ratio":1.5233333333333334,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caeberllan_Cawrfab_7fed%27,_the_best_Welsh_Black_bullock_in_Smithfield_Show,_London_1973_(1519770).jpg","share":0.2175},{"title":"Caeberllan